# Build artifacts
build/
install/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Tool caches. Note that listing a pattern here does NOT untrack files already
# committed: the 39 .pyc under __pycache__/ matched the rules above for a long
# time and stayed in the repo regardless, until they were removed from the index.
# Check with: git ls-files -i -c --exclude-standard
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ROOT files (large binary data — use EOS or CERNBox instead)
*.root

# Compiled shared libraries
*.so
*.so.*
*.a
*.dylib

# Python virtual environments
.venv*/

# Simulation output data
simulation/run_script/data/
simulation/run_script/log/
simulation/run_script/steer/*.mac
simulation/run_script/steer

# Tests
simulation/geometry/general_tests

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Calibration payloads that no code in this repo reads. The MIP tables under
# masking_info/calibration/MuonCalib_gaudi/mips/ ARE tracked -- the masking has to
# work from this repo alone, without assuming siwecal-tb2026 sits next to it.
# Pedestals and LG->HG anchors are a different matter: tens of MB that nothing
# here opens, produced and versioned in siwecal-tb2026, so they stay out.
masking_info/calibration/**/pedestals/
masking_info/calibration/**/anchor/

# Working notes for the tracking rework — never commit
instructions_opus.md

# Personal notes with hardcoded EOS example paths — never commit
docs/ejemplos_tracking.md
